Two useful integration levels

Level 1 — ChatGPT GitHub connection: I can read the live repository, inspect chapters, compare versions, analyze your structure, and reference existing files. It cannot push changes.

Level 2 — Codex connection: Codex can work on files, prepare changes, create branches, and open pull requests. This is the integration you want for maintaining the living book.

You can also install Codex locally on Windows and run it from inside the cloned Project Ascent folder. The official Codex CLI supports signing in with a ChatGPT account and working directly from your terminal.

For this project, I recommend Codex cloud plus pull requests, with the root AGENTS.md above. That gives us the closest practical version of putting Atlas directly inside Mission Control.

